================================================================================
SUMMARY
================================================================================

This repository is a starter template that may include a vendored copy of the
ForgEng engine under src/vendor/forgeng/ (or equivalent paths).

- Template / game code: free to use and improve for client-side games.
- ForgEng engine: not licensed for installation on other computers, and not
  licensed for commercial use.

The full terms below control if anything in this summary conflicts.

================================================================================
1. DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

"Template Code" means the application, scene, UI, build, and documentation
files in this repository that are not the Engine.

"Engine" means ForgEng itself and any vendored engine runtime, shaders,
contracts, DomUiShell, presets, or related binaries/sources shipped under
vendor paths in this repository (for example src/vendor/forgeng/).

"Client-Side Game" means an interactive game or demo that runs in an end-user
client environment (for example a web browser), including local development
and non-commercial playtesting of that game.

"Commercial Use" means any use intended for or resulting in commercial
advantage or monetary compensation, including selling, licensing, SaaS,
paid hosting of the Engine, paid redistribution, or embedding the Engine in
a paid product or service — except where Section 2 expressly allows you to
ship a Client-Side Game that merely embeds the Engine as a dependency of
that game under the limits of this license.

================================================================================
2. TEMPLATE CODE — PERMITTED USE
================================================================================

Subject to Section 3 and Section 4, you may freely:

  a) use, copy, modify, and improve the Template Code;
  b) build and further develop Client-Side Games based on the Template Code;
  c) distribute your Client-Side Games that include Template Code changes.

================================================================================
3. ENGINE — STRICT RESTRICTIONS
================================================================================

The Engine is proprietary to ForgEngDev unless a separate written license
from ForgEngDev says otherwise.

You MUST NOT:

  a) install, copy, deploy, host, or redistribute the Engine onto or for other
     computers, servers, devices, or users as a standalone engine, SDK,
     toolkit, or development environment;
  b) use the Engine for Commercial Use;
  c) extract the Engine from this template to create another engine
     distribution, mirror, fork-as-engine, or competing runtime package;
  d) remove, obscure, or alter Engine copyright, attribution, or license
     notices.

Limited exception for game shipping:
You may embed the Engine only as needed for your own Client-Side Game to run
for end users, provided that embedding is not Commercial Use of the Engine
and does not grant those end users rights to use the Engine as a development
tool or to reinstall/redistribute the Engine separately.

If you need commercial rights or multi-machine Engine installation rights,
contact ForgEngDev for a separate license.

